# Every process settings page, asserted by a label only that page shows.
#
# The six pages live in the left panel's tab strip, and the panel is only wide
# enough for five of them, so the panel is widened first and the widen is proven
# by finding "Others" rather than assumed. The tabs are clicked by coordinate:
# a tab that is not selected is painted grey on dark and no OCR pass reads it,
# which is why the page is asserted instead of the tab. Each page is waited for
# rather than sampled once -- a page that is still building reads as missing.
#
# The first lines clear whatever Orca raised about its own recent projects and
# make sure the Prepare view is the one on screen: a modal stops every tab click
# behind it, and a cold start lands on the home screen, which has no settings
# panel at all. Both are forgiven so the drive still runs on a clean profile.
try key enter --window Error
window '*OrcaSlicer*'
try click-text Prepare
sleep 3
wait-text "Process" --timeout 40
drag 392 600 660 600 --steps 12
assert-text "Others"
sleep 0.5
click 43 380
wait-text "Layer height" --timeout 10
sleep 0.4
click 126 380
wait-text "Wall loops" --timeout 10
sleep 0.4
click 210 380
wait-text "First layer speed" --timeout 10
sleep 0.4
click 289 380
wait-text "Enable support" --timeout 10
sleep 0.4
click 392 380
wait-text "Prime tower" --timeout 10
sleep 0.4
click 492 380
wait-text "Skirt" --timeout 10
sleep 0.4
click 43 380
drag 660 600 392 600 --steps 12
